WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:03.340
Abraham: So how does Cyber
crime affect the individual?

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:07.670
As individuals we can have
our finances and social status

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:09.600
heavily impacted by cyber crime.

00:00:10.599 --> 00:00:14.069
Unsolicited emails and texts and
those often pertaining to be from

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:18.189
our own bank or the Inland Revenue
can have consequences when interacted

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:20.110
with which may be financial.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:24.370
Once details have been unwittingly
given, the cyber criminals have

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:28.750
access to more than just our details,
they can access bank accounts and

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:30.849
commit crimes using our identity.

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:35.909
This can then expand into our social
media circles or work-based contacts.

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:40.060
Phones and smart technology around
the home can be hacked and taken

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:43.530
control of with the opportunity
for being surveilled by cameras.

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:48.470
Having 'up to date’ antimalware software
and making sure all programs are up to

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:50.469
date can help to keep systems secure.

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:56.319
Also taking extra precautions like having
good password protection, cautious when

00:00:56.329 --> 00:01:01.660
giving out details online, only accessing
secure sites, keeping phones and storage

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:06.479
devices safe and away from prying eyes and
being careful with any documentation that

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:08.740
may have details on it and destroying it.

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:12.059
Nicole: Let’s now look at
how it can affect Businesses.

00:01:12.059 --> 00:01:17.970
Cybercrime can devastate a company’s
finances and reputation quickly

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:21.590
or can cause a great deal of
disruption to an organisation.

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:27.380
In the long term it can cause irreparable
financial or brand damage, or even

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:29.520
threaten an individual’s way of life.

00:01:30.379 --> 00:01:34.490
Companies need to realise what a
threat cyber crime is and to stop

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:38.000
their business falling victim to
the cyber criminals should invest

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:40.529
in reliable cyber security services.

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:46.729
A DDoS cyber attack involves a network
being flooded with excessive traffic

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:50.830
causing it to shut down and becoming
unavailable to legitimate users.

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:55.199
Hacking involves the cybercriminal
in trying to take advantage

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:58.470
of vulnerabilities in a
company’s software and systems.

00:01:59.289 --> 00:02:03.820
Hackers will ask for a ransom to end
the attack, however by using trusted

00:02:03.849 --> 00:02:08.239
and reliable technology service
providers, increasing bandwidth, and

00:02:08.289 --> 00:02:13.220
designing systems to scale with traffic
using the cloud this can be prevented.

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:18.280
There is also a significant impact to
the business from regulatory bodies.

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:22.940
An example of this would be British
Airways who were fined £20 million

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:27.397
one of the highest under GDPR by the
ICO for their lack of due diligence

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:36.179
that led to the compromise of
429,612 staff and customer details.

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:40.179
Abraham: The effects of cybercrime
can be minimised by businesses making

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:44.319
employees aware and wary of downloading
attachments or clicking on links

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:48.500
to reset passwords without knowing
exactly who they have come from or

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:50.590
checking their authenticity directly.

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:54.460
Personal information and contact details
should not be given freely, so as to

00:02:54.469 --> 00:02:56.079
give access to hackers and scammers.

00:02:57.049 --> 00:03:00.770
Businesses should also limit the amount of
information they put out on their website.

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:07.140
Passwords should be long, complex, and
original for each individual account.

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:12.349
They should not be easy to identify from
personal information, for example, not the

00:03:12.349 --> 00:03:17.859
name of a child or pet, or based on the
month or season of the year ‘Summer2021’.

00:03:19.219 --> 00:03:23.250
These sorts of password relatedly come
up on the list of most common passwords.

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:27.630
To minimise insider attacks all
data storage should be encrypted

00:03:27.679 --> 00:03:30.680
and software should be updated
regularly to maintain security.

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:34.209
Companies can also enforce two-factor
authentication for all their user

00:03:34.209 --> 00:03:37.730
accounts so that attackers are less
likely to be able to gain access

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:39.380
even with the right credentials.

00:03:39.910 --> 00:03:42.079
Nicole: So how are nations affected?

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:45.579
Nation state attacks are
usually thought of as highly

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:47.429
complex, and technology based.

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:52.839
However social engineering is commonly
used to convince individuals to download

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:55.050
malware to create security breaches.

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:59.600
“Spear Phishing' attacks are often
used to infiltrate, inserting

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:04.020
malware which may remain dormant
until triggered by an outside agency

00:04:04.059 --> 00:04:06.090
making it difficult to guard against.

00:04:06.809 --> 00:04:10.440
State-backed actors are responsible
for gaining access to computer

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:11.969
networks around the world.

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:17.419
Countries like China seem intent on
committing large scale espionage even

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:23.390
though as part of the G20 they agreed not
to conduct or support cyber enabled theft

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:26.159
of intellectual property or personal data.

00:04:26.849 --> 00:04:32.490
In the UK The National Cyber Security
Centre [NCSC] supports the government

00:04:32.490 --> 00:04:37.020
giving advice to organisations affected
by state run cyber intrusions stealing

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:42.909
trade secrets such as those by the Chinese
Ministry of State Security [MSS] in 2018.

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:47.859
Abraham: To guard against these often
changing and increasingly sophisticated

00:04:47.859 --> 00:04:51.969
attacks, organisations must have a
multi-layered approach to their cyber

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:57.530
security [referred to as “defence in
depth”], creating nation state threat

00:04:57.570 --> 00:05:02.470
risk models and educating employees on
being hyper aware of nation state attacks.

00:05:03.309 --> 00:05:07.430
They also need to be constantly aware of
the threat and training should be ongoing.

